{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>See, I have set before you this day</b> — He returns to admonish them further, to declare to them that both paths are in their hands, and it is within their authority to walk in whichever they desire, and there is no impediment or obstacle in their hands, neither from those below nor from those above. And he calls the heavens and the earth to witness against them a second time (Deuteronomy 30:19), after he already said (Deuteronomy 4:26), \"I call the heavens and the earth to witness against you this day that you will surely perish quickly\" — for now he says, \"I call the heavens and the earth to witness against you this day, that I have set life and death before you,\" which are the blessing and the curse, \"and that I have counseled you to choose life, so that you and your seed may live.\" And behold, this is like ratifying the witnesses at the conclusion of all his words."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:01.153053412Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}